#+TITLE: Owned COM close fails after native tests and RESTORED
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation
#+BRANCH: codex/alfe-com-job-drawing

* Evidence
SCHME !339 job 564957 executes all 23 local historical assertions successfully
with ALFE 2.3.83. The protocol reaches RESTORED, but close-owned.result is 1
and the owned AutoCAD remains alive, blocking profile restoration. The emitted
bridge attempts Document.Close and Quit only once, then waits for process exit
while retaining its COM references. It discards the original COM error.
The exact reason for this native close rejection remains to be confirmed.

* Correction under qualification
Retry document closure and Quit at most 40 times, 250 ms apart; preserve the
COM error, release owned automation references, and still require captured
PID/creation identity disappearance. Never attach to or kill another instance.
Persistent failure must remain a nonzero CLI result. Attached sessions stay open.
